{:href "/athletes/126186"} "Cameron McEvoy"] " won in 47.04, the second fastest time ever after " [:a {:href ""} "Cesar Cielo"] "’s high-tech suit world record of 46.91 from 2009. McEvoy’s time was almost 7/10ths faster than any other time in 2016. China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/133209"} "Ning Zetao"] " had won the 2015 World Championships in somewhat of an upset but was a contender, as was American " [:a {:href "/athletes/115617"} "Nathan Adrian"] ", the defending gold medalist, who won the US Olympic Trials. Other challengers were thought to be Russian " [:a {:href ""} "Vladimir Morozov"] " and France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/125884"} "Florent Manaudou"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the end, nothing went according to form in this race, even before Rio, as Manaudou failed to qualify for the French team in the event. Zetao made the semi-finals but failed to qualify for the final. McEvoy made the final but never found his way, finished seventh, and had to watch his countryman, " [:a {:href "/athletes/132557"} "Kyle Chalmers"] ", win a major upset gold medal. Chalmers was seventh at the turn, but finished the strongest to win in 47.58, a world junior record. Behind him, the silver went to unheralded Belgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/126406"} "Pieter Timmers"] ", while Adrian won bronze."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/132557"} "Kyle Chalmers"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "47.90 (1 h7)"] [:td {} "47.88 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "47.58 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126406"} "Pieter Timmers